  "title": "Balancing Uncertainty and Diversity in Active Learning Frameworks for Object Detection",
  "summary": "This study proposes a hybrid sampling method to balance uncertainty and diversity in active learning, enhancing the effectiveness of the framework by selecting both uncertain and diverse samples. The method improves model performance through better feature learning and labeling efficiency, while maintaining robustness during training.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The proposed method, Least Confident and Diverse (LCD), improves model performance by selecting uncertain and diverse samples.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The study uses experiments on complex datasets to evaluate the efficacy of the LCD method, showing improvements in both image-based and object-based evaluations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The algorithm is available for implementation at the GitHub repository: https://github.com/vipularya135/LCD",
      "confidence": 0.95
